<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Config for MissionAccessibilityService, referenced from AndroidManifest.xml via
    <meta-data android:name="android.accessibilityservice" android:resource="@xml/mission_accessibility_service_config" />.

    This is the ANDROID FRAMEWORK'S required static declaration (shown in device Settings >
    Accessibility when the user enables the service) — a separate thing from the Play Console
    declaration/use-case-justification text Architecture doc §1.2 requires before a *store*
    submission. That store-declaration work remains explicitly out of scope for this pass per
    ROADMAP.md's Phase 2 entry (sideload-only distribution today) and is NOT drafted here —
    this file's android:description below is deliberately plain, on-device Settings copy only,
    not an attempt at Play Console review copy.

    android:accessibilityEventTypes/feedbackType/notificationTimeout here mirror what
    MissionAccessibilityService.onServiceConnected() already sets programmatically on
    `serviceInfo` at runtime — Android requires SOME static declaration in this file
    regardless (the framework reads it before onServiceConnected() ever runs, e.g. to render
    the service in Settings), so the two are kept in sync rather than one being authoritative
    and the other stale. If the runtime AccessibilityServiceInfo config in the Kotlin file
    ever changes, this file needs the matching update — noting that explicitly since it's an
    easy thing to let drift.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:notificationTimeout="100"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="false"
    android:description="@string/accessibility_service_description"
    android:summary="@string/accessibility_service_summary" />
